# config/Kconfig.brain — Brain server link defaults and subsumption layer enables
#
# RFC-0026 Phase C1.  Compile-time defaults for the brain link.
# Runtime values can be overridden in CONFIG.INI.
#
# Sourced from inside the Robot menu (config/Kconfig.robot), so it is shown
# only for DOMAIN_ROBOT. The brain-link task is compiled only into a
# DOMAIN_ROBOT image (kernel feature `domain-robot`, wave 11); its two
# enforcement switches in "Security" depend on DOMAIN_ROBOT.

menu "Brain Server Link"
config MULTISTREAM_SCHED_PRIORITY
    bool "Multi-stream scheduler: priority (control preempts bulk)"
    default n
    help
      RFC-0021 multi-stream link scheduling policy — a compile-time
      choice so each binary carries exactly one policy (zero hot-path
      overhead; the unused branch is const-eliminated).

      n (default) = FIFO: streams share the link in send order; a large
        STREAM_CAMERA frame can head-of-line-block a STREAM_CONTROL frame.
      y = PRIORITY: STREAM_CONTROL frames are interleaved ahead of bulk
        stream chunks, bounding control hold-off to ~one chunk-time
        instead of one full bulk-frame-time (experiment I2).

      Selected via `make menuconfig` / defconfig; surfaces as
      `azos_limits::MULTISTREAM_SCHED_PRIORITY`. A/B the two builds
      with the bench_boot capture + dashboard. Outside DOMAIN_ROBOT the
      option is hidden and reads as n (FIFO).

endmenu # Brain Server Link
